Decorate the given method as line magic.

The decorator can be used with or without arguments, as follows.

i) without arguments: it will create a line magic named as the method being
decorated::

    @deco
    def foo(...)

will create a line magic named `foo`.

ii) with one string argument: which will be used as the actual name of the
resulting magic::

    @deco('bar')
    def foo(...)

will create a line magic named `bar`.

To register a class magic use ``Interactiveshell.register_magic(class or instance)``.

Each node represents a function.
qualified_name: string which represents the namespace/name of the function
abstract_syntax_tree: subtree of the overall module which corresponds to this function

qualified_name is of the structure: (namespace1, namespace2, ..., name)

For example, foo() in the following would be represented as (A, B, foo):

class A:
    class B:
        def foo():
            pass

